<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Bonnita year earnings fall, holds div.</title>
<headline>Bonnita year earnings fall, holds div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended April 30, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		27.2	  vs 30.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  9.5	  vs  same</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   60.04	 vs 64.83</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   88.86	 vs 95.77</p>
<p>    Tax			 28.76	 vs 30.94</p>
<p>    Interest earned	  2.67	 vs paid 0.69</p>
<p>    Turnover	     1,038.49	 vs 960.74</p>
<p>Div payable Aug 6</p>
<p>on register July 25</p>
<p>Full name: Bonnita Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Dairy group Bonnita said its results had been affected by a shortage of milk.</p>
<p>A new factory would be established in Gauteng this year, giving the group access to another 40 percent of the country's raw milk. It expected high milk prices to continue affecting profit margings, but was confident that market forces would prevail.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
